        {
          "id": "p1",
          "text": "In May 2026, the Visayas region faced a major power shortfall after a critical piece of energy infrastructure failed. With seasonal heat driving demand into a thin operating margin, the grid was put on high alert. To prevent a bigger crisis, authorities mandated power cuts, leaving over 950 megawatts unavailable for ordinary households and businesses struggling in the heat.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
            "fragments": [
              "why-2",
              "how-1",
              "how-2",
              "result-0"
            ],
            "center": "result-0",
            "channel": "toned",
            "channel_role": "toned",
            "composition_mode": "ADR-0008"
          },
          "warnings": [],
          "fit": 0.85
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "text": "When a machine everyone depends on suddenly broke down, it was the beginning of a tense period for the everyday workers keeping the lights on. They watched as ongoing shutdowns at other plants and we all turning up the air conditioning created a crisis. The power managers issued a warning, but the system couldn't handle the demand, forcing them to cut power to prevent a bigger outage that would have hit our community even harder.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
            "fragments": [
              "why-0",
              "why-1",
              "why-2",
              "how-1",
              "how-2"
            ],
            "center": "who-1",
            "channel": "focalized",
            "channel_role": "focalized",
            "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
            "focal": "who-1"
          },
          "warnings": [],
          "fit": 0.78
        },
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "text": "The power grid managers had to respond to the failing infrastructure caused by a major power plant breaking down. With high summer demand straining the system, they declared an emergency for our region. The local power plants we all rely on were already offline, leading to a huge loss of power for ordinary people and rolling blackouts as authorities tried to stabilize the grid.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
