        {
          "id": "p1",
          "text": "Faced with a massive power deficit to overcome, decisive crisis managers moved swiftly. After the critical system failure of Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2 and compounded by extended plant shutdowns, the authorities declared a red alert for the island group. They then implemented the courageous decision to prevent total collapse, ordering emergency load shedding to stabilize the grid and avert a wider energy deficit.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Hero",
            "fragments": [
              "why-0",
              "why-1",
              "how-1",
              "how-2",
              "result-0"
            ],
            "center": "result-0",
            "channel": "toned",
            "channel_role": "toned",
            "composition_mode": "ADR-0008"
          },
          "warnings": [
            "ignored focal 'None' on toned channel"
          ],
          "fit": 0.85
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "text": "We saw the high demand from seasonal heat push the system to its limit. Our generators were already offline. When the critical equipment failure hit our power unit, we faced an impossible choice. To protect the wider grid from collapse, we had to make a drastic, painful measure. We ordered the emergency load reduction, knowing it would cause significant loss of generation capacity but preventing a total blackout.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Hero",
            "fragments": [
              "why-2",
              "why-1",
              "why-0",
              "how-2",
              "result-0"
            ],
            "center": "how-2",
            "channel": "focalized",
            "channel_role": "focalized",
            "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
            "focal": "who-2"
          },
          "warnings": [],
          "fit": 0.78
        },
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "text": "The grid guardians faced an unexpected shutdown that cascaded into a full crisis. With seasonal heat driving demand into a thin operating margin, the initial failure exposed deep system vulnerabilities. Their emergency response was a high-level warning, a red alert for the affected region, to manage the sudden shortage and prevent a catastrophic overload of critical transmission lines.",
