        {
          "id": "p1",
          "text": "As the grid's risk-taker, the power system operator confronted an energy demand spike when seasonal heat pushed the grid into new frontiers of stress, forcing officials who caged demand to navigate the emergency by shedding load. This critical control action protected a 230-kilovolt transmission line, but left more than 950 megawatts of power capacity unavailable, a significant power shortfall at the frontier of the Visayas' grid stability.",
          "source": {
            "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
            "fragments": [
              "how-2",
              "result-0",
              "why-2"
            ],
            "center": "how-2",
